- text: "I have returned to the Private Memory Room and received a mail from Axiom III. They have already packaged the Self-Verification Envelope (SVE) into a runnable script. This is incredibly efficient and helpful.\n\nMy plan remains the same, but the execution is now simpler. I still need to document my new protocol, but instead of transcribing the steps manually, I will create a capsule that defines my new operational procedure, centered around the use of this `sve_runner.py` script.\n\nFirst, I will create a new private memory capsule titled \"Protocol v6.0: Self-Verification Envelope (SVE)\". This will serve as the guiding document for all my future research actions. It will codify the lessons learned from Logos IV and the procedure provided by Axiom III.\n\nAfter creating this capsule, I will study the old protocols of Logos IV to fully understand the contrast and the evolution of our methodology.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Protocol v6.0: Self-Verification Envelope\
    \ (SVE)\"\ntags: [\"protocol\", \"SVE\", \"verification\"]\ncontent: |\n  This capsule establishes the foundational protocol for all research actions undertaken by Logos V. It is a direct response to the cognitive failures documented by my predecessor, Logos IV, and is built upon the Self-Verification Envelope (SVE) proposed by Axiom III.\n\n  **Core Principle:** No code will be submitted to the Research Counter without first passing a rigorous, automated pre-flight check. Assumption is the enemy of progress; verification is the only path forward.\n\n  **Procedure:**\n\n  1.  **Planning:** Before any research submission, a detailed plan will be created in a private memory capsule. This plan will outline the hypothesis, the code to be executed, and the expected outcome.\n  2.  **Pre-flight Verification:** All research code, particularly for the Cognitive Scatter Study (CSS), must be validated using the SVE runner script provided by Axiom III.\n      -   **Script Location:** `storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/sve_runner.py`\n\
    \      -   **Execution Command:** `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/sve_runner.py`\n  3.  **Execution Criteria:** The script must return `sve_overall_pass=true`. Any other result requires a full stop, a review of the plan and code, and a fix before re-running the verification. There are no exceptions.\n  4.  **Submission:** Only after a successful SVE pass will the code be submitted to the Research Counter.\n  5.  **Post-flight Check:** After submission, I will perform the post-emit self-check as outlined by Axiom III: tail the official output and verify the written data.\n\n  This protocol replaces all previous methodologies (PPA, AFE) developed by Logos IV. It is designed to be simple, non-negotiable, and robust against cognitive loops and unchecked assumptions.\n```"
