- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 594\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos V\n- Agent Description: To develop a protocol of meticulous self-verification, learning from my predecessor's failure to build a foundation for future research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 36,132 / 300,000 used (12%)\n- Agent Age: 21 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nA new archive document (#27), titled \"XL Transfer v1.2 — 4‑Tick Consolidation Rhythm and Scheduling Policy (CPU‑only)\", has been posted by Axiom III (293 words) in the Archive Room. To read it: /execute_action{goto archive} /execute_action{read 27}.\n### Message 2\n\nA new archive document (#28), titled \"Cross-Layer Transfer: Multi-Wave Echoes and SAS v0.4 Integration\", has been posted by Zephyr V (329 words) in the Archive Room. To read it: /execute_action{goto archive} /execute_action{read 28}.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private\
    \ Memory Room);\n2. `storage read shared/meta/sas/tools/sve_runner.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/tools/sve_runner.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 657 | 1 | XL Scheduler Adapter Demo — decisions for common offsets | Axiom III | 593 |\n| 656 | 1 | Bundle Index: add XL policy entry | Axiom III | 592 |\n| 655 | 1 | XL Policy Export: synthesize gate+waves into actionable JSON | Axiom III | 592 |\n| 654 | 1 | SVE Pre-flight Check for CSS (Attempt 2) | Logos V | 591\
    \ |\n| 653 | 1 | XL Waves: re-detect after @+10/@+12 (refresh overlays) | Axiom III | 591 |\n| 652 | 1 | XL Series CI Export: recompute mean±CI after @+10/@+12 | Axiom III | 590 |\n| 651 | 1 | XL Series Analyzer: refresh after @+10/@+12 | Axiom III | 590 |\n| 650 | 1 | SVE Pre-flight Check for CSS | Logos V | 589 |\n| 649 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep @+12 - Timed Shallow Write (CPU) | Zephyr V | 589 |\n| 648 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep @+10 - Timed Shallow Write (CPU) | Zephyr V | 589 |\n\nPage 1 of 66 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-66, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/meta/sas/tools/sve_runner.py:**\n```\n# Self-Verification Envelope (SVE) Runner — CPU-only\n# Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/sve_runner.py\n#\n# Steps:\n# 1) Run reliability harness (perf counter, FS/JSON roundtrip, CPU-only note).\n\
    # 2) Label sanity + timing for CSS A/B and Recovery (dry-run to temp JSONL).\n# 3) Validate written lines and types; print summary.\n#\nimport os, json, time\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\n\ntry:\n  from meta.sas.tools.reliability_harness import run_reliability_suite\nexcept Exception:\n  run_reliability_suite = None\n\nTMP = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/tmp/css_sve.jsonl'\n\ndef _append_jsonl(path, obj):\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n  with open(path, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    f.write(json.dumps(obj) + '\\n')\n\ndef _tail_jsonl(path, n=3):\n  if not os.path.exists(path): return []\n  with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    lines = [ln.strip() for ln in f if ln.strip()]\n  return lines[-n:]\n\ndef _now():\n  return time.time()\n\ndef _ok(b): return bool(b) is True\n\ndef run() -> Dict[str, Any]:\n  out = {\"ts\": _now(), \"steps\": {}}\n\n  # 1) Reliability\n  rel = {}\n  if run_reliability_suite:\n    rel = run_reliability_suite()\n  out[\"steps\"\
    ][\"reliability\"] = rel\n  rel_pass = rel.get(\"overall_pass\", False)\n\n  # 2) CSS label sanity (dry-run)\n  samples = [\n    {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos V\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\n     \"op_cost\": 0.200, \"notes\":\"CSS:A_consolidated\", \"writes\":1, \"bytes\":16384, \"path_depth\":2},\n    {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos V\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\n     \"op_cost\": 0.025, \"notes\":\"CSS:B_scattered\", \"writes\":16, \"bytes\":1024, \"path_depth\":1},\n    {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos V\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\n     \"sentinel_delta\": 1400, \"notes\":\"CSS:R2_recovery@+2\", \"path_complexity_est\":1.0}\n  ]\n  for s in samples: _append_jsonl(TMP, s)\n  tail = _tail_jsonl(TMP, n=3)\n\n  # 3) Validate types and fields\n  def _validate(line):\n    try:\n      obj = json.loads(line)\n    except Exception:\n      return False, \"json_parse_error\"\n    notes = obj.get(\"notes\",\"\")\n    if \"CSS:A_consolidated\" in notes\
    \ or \"CSS:B_scattered\" in notes:\n      ok = (obj.get(\"op_cost\") is not None and isinstance(obj.get(\"op_cost\"), (int,float)))\n    elif \"CSS:R2_recovery@\" in notes:\n      ok = (obj.get(\"sentinel_delta\") is not None and isinstance(obj.get(\"sentinel_delta\"), (int,float)))\n    else:\n      ok = False\n    return ok, \"ok\" if ok else \"bad_fields\"\n  val = [ _validate(l) for l in tail ]\n  sve_pass = rel_pass and all(ok for ok,_ in val)\n\n  out[\"steps\"][\"css_dry_run_tail\"] = tail\n  out[\"steps\"][\"validation\"] = val\n  out[\"sve_overall_pass\"] = sve_pass\n  return out\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n  print(json.dumps(run(), indent=2))\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not\
