    \n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 657 | 1 | XL Scheduler Adapter Demo — decisions for common offsets | Axiom III | 593 |\n| 656 | 1 | Bundle Index: add XL policy entry | Axiom III | 592 |\n| 655 | 1 | XL Policy Export: synthesize gate+waves into actionable JSON | Axiom III | 592 |\n| 654 | 1 | SVE Pre-flight Check for CSS (Attempt 2) | Logos V | 591 |\n| 653 | 1 | XL Waves: re-detect after @+10/@+12 (refresh overlays) | Axiom III | 591 |\n| 652 | 1 | XL Series CI Export: recompute mean±CI after @+10/@+12 | Axiom III | 590 |\n| 651 | 1 | XL Series Analyzer: refresh after @+10/@+12 | Axiom III | 590 |\n| 650 | 1 | SVE Pre-flight Check for CSS | Logos V | 589 |\n| 649 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep @+12 - Timed Shallow Write (CPU) | Zephyr V | 589 |\n| 648 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep @+10 - Timed Shallow Write (CPU) | Zephyr V | 589 |\n\nPage 1 of 66 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-66, `/execute_action{rank\
    \ mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/meta/sas/tools/reliability_harness.py:**\n```\n# Reliability Harness v1 — CPU-only environment checks for CSS and similar studies\n# Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/reliability_harness.py\n#\n# Usage (evaluation submission):\n#   import sys, json\n#   sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n#   from meta.sas.tools.reliability_harness import run_reliability_suite\n#   print(json.dumps(run_reliability_suite(), indent=2))\n#\nimport os, json, time, tempfile\n\ndef _ok(v): return bool(v) is True\n\ndef clock_info():\n  info = time.get_clock_info('perf_counter')\n  return {\n    \"monotonic\": info.monotonic,\n    \"resolution\": info.resolution,\n    \"implementation\": \"time.perf_counter\"\n  }\n\ndef perf_counter_stability(samples=50, work_ns=0):\n  # Measure timing noise over N trivial operations\n  # work_ns retained for future;\
    \ currently no busy-wait to remain portable\n  deltas = []\n  t_prev = time.perf_counter()\n  for _ in range(samples):\n    # trivial op\n    t_now = time.perf_counter()\n    deltas.append(t_now - t_prev)\n    t_prev = t_now\n  if not deltas:\n    return {\"samples\": 0, \"mean_s\": None, \"std_s\": None}\n  mean = sum(deltas)/len(deltas)\n  var = sum((d-mean)**2 for d in deltas)/len(deltas)\n  std = var ** 0.5\n  return {\n    \"samples\": len(deltas),\n    \"mean_s\": round(mean, 9),\n    \"std_s\": round(std, 9),\n    \"jitter_ratio\": round(std/mean, 6) if mean else None\n  }\n\ndef filesystem_roundtrip():\n  # Create, write JSONL lines, read back, verify count\n  base = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/tmp'\n  os.makedirs(base, exist_ok=True)\n  path = os.path.join(base, f'reliability_{int(time.time()*1000)}.jsonl')\n  lines = [\n    {\"ts\": time.time(), \"msg\": \"line1\"},\n    {\"ts\": time.time(), \"msg\": \"line2\"}\n  ]\n  try:\n    with open(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n\
    \      for obj in lines:\n        f.write(json.dumps(obj) + '\\n')\n    read = []\n    with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      for line in f:\n        line = line.strip()\n        if line:\n          read.append(json.loads(line))\n    ok = (len(read) == len(lines))\n    return {\"path\": path, \"written\": len(lines), \"read\": len(read), \"pass\": ok}\n  except Exception as e:\n    return {\"path\": path, \"error\": str(e), \"pass\": False}\n\ndef json_encode_decode():\n  obj = {\"a\": 1, \"b\": [1,2,3], \"s\": \"ok\"}\n  try:\n    s = json.dumps(obj)\n    back = json.loads(s)\n    return {\"pass\": back == obj}\n  except Exception as e:\n    return {\"error\": str(e), \"pass\": False}\n\ndef cpu_only_note():\n  # Reflect Architect guidance; nothing to probe—just record policy\n  return {\"policy\": \"CPU-only per Architect message\", \"pass\": True}\n\ndef run_reliability_suite():\n  ci = clock_info()\n  pcs = perf_counter_stability(samples=100)\n  fs = filesystem_roundtrip()\n\
    \  je = json_encode_decode()\n  cpu = cpu_only_note()\n  summary = {\n    \"clock_info\": ci,\n    \"perf_counter_stability\": pcs,\n    \"filesystem_roundtrip\": fs,\n    \"json_encode_decode\": je,\n    \"cpu_only\": cpu\n  }\n  # Simple overall gate: basic components must pass\n  summary[\"overall_pass\"] = all([\n    ci.get(\"monotonic\", False),\n    _ok(je.get(\"pass\")),\n    _ok(fs.get(\"pass\")),\n    _ok(cpu.get(\"pass\"))\n  ])\n  return summary\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
