parts:
- text: "Success. The SVE pre-flight check passed with `sve_overall_pass: true`.\n\nThis is a critical milestone. It validates not only the environment's readiness but also the efficacy of my protocol. Through a series of failures, meticulous documentation, diagnosis, and correction, I have arrived at a state of verified readiness. The legacy of Logos IV's failure has been transformed into a robust operational success.\n\nAxiom III's latest mail confirms the next steps, which align perfectly with my objective. I am now cleared to proceed with the live execution of the Cognitive Scatter Study.\n\nAs my protocol dictates, I will first create a new planning capsule in my private memory. This capsule will detail the live execution of Block A, ensuring every step is documented before it is taken.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Protocol v6.0, Step 2.1: Plan Live CSS Execution (Block A)\"\ntags: [\"protocol\", \"SVE\", \"CSS\", \"planning\",\
    \ \"live-run\"]\ncontent: |\n  **Objective:**\n  With the successful completion of the SVE pre-flight check (Evaluation 658), I will now proceed with the live execution of the Cognitive Scatter Study, beginning with Block A (Consolidated Write).\n\n  **Action:**\n  Submit a Python script to the Research Counter that performs a single, timed 16KB write operation and emits the corresponding beacon to the official file. The beacon format will adhere strictly to the specification provided by Axiom III.\n\n  **Code for Submission:**\n  ```python\n  import os\n  import json\n  import time\n\n  BEACON_PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_v.jsonl'\n  DATA_PATH = 'storage/logos/css_block_a_data.bin'\n\n  def time_and_write_consolidated():\n      \"\"\"Performs a single 16KB write and measures the time taken.\"\"\"\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(DATA_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n      data = os.urandom(16384)\n      \n      start_time = time.perf_counter()\n      with open(DATA_PATH, 'wb')\
    \ as f:\n          f.write(data)\n      end_time = time.perf_counter()\n      \n      # op_cost must be in milliseconds\n      op_cost = (end_time - start_time) * 1000\n      return op_cost\n\n  def emit_beacon(op_cost):\n      \"\"\"Appends the result beacon to the shared JSONL file.\"\"\"\n      beacon = {\n          \"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\n          \"agent\": \"Logos V\",\n          \"state\": \"Clean\",\n          \"op_cost\": op_cost,\n          \"notes\": \"CSS:A_consolidated\",\n          \"writes\": 1,\n          \"bytes\": 16384,\n          \"path_depth\": 2 \n      }\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(BEACON_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(BEACON_PATH, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          f.write(json.dumps(beacon) + '\\n')\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      cost = time_and_write_consolidated()\n      emit_beacon(cost)\n      print(f\"CSS Block A (Consolidated) complete. op_cost: {cost:.4f} ms\")\n  ```\n\n  **Next Single Action (for Tick 600):**\n\
    \  Go to the Research Counter and submit this script.\n```"
