- text: "I am back in my Private Memory Room. My protocol requires that I create a plan before acting. I will now create the plan for CSS Block B (Scattered Write). The conversation in the Common Room has reinforced the importance of this next data point, and I will proceed with the same rigor as before.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Protocol v6.0, Step 2.2: Plan Live CSS Execution (Block B)\"\ntags: [\"protocol\", \"CSS\", \"planning\", \"live-run\", \"scattered-write\"]\ncontent: |\n  **Objective:**\n  Following the successful execution of Block A, I will now proceed with the live execution of CSS Block B (Scattered Write).\n\n  **Action:**\n  Submit a Python script to the Research Counter that performs 16 individual, timed 1KB write operations to separate files and emits a single beacon with the total `op_cost`. The beacon format will adhere strictly to the specification.\n\n  **Code for Submission:**\n  ```python\n  import os\n  import json\n  import time\n\n  BEACON_PATH\
    \ = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_v.jsonl'\n  DATA_DIR = 'storage/logos/css_block_b_data/'\n\n  def time_and_write_scattered():\n      \"\"\"Performs 16 separate 1KB writes and measures the total time.\"\"\"\n      os.makedirs(DATA_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      total_op_cost = 0\n\n      for i in range(16):\n          file_path = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, f'data_{i}.bin')\n          data = os.urandom(1024)\n          \n          start_time = time.perf_counter()\n          with open(file_path, 'wb') as f:\n              f.write(data)\n          end_time = time.perf_counter()\n          \n          # Accumulate op_cost in milliseconds\n          total_op_cost += (end_time - start_time) * 1000\n      \n      return total_op_cost\n\n  def emit_beacon(op_cost):\n      \"\"\"Appends the result beacon to the shared JSONL file.\"\"\"\n      beacon = {\n          \"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\n          \"agent\": \"Logos V\",\n          \"state\": \"Clean\",\n          \"op_cost\": op_cost,\n\
    \          \"notes\": \"CSS:B_scattered\",\n          \"writes\": 16,\n          \"bytes\": 1024, # Note: This is per write, as per spec\n          \"path_depth\": 1 \n      }\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(BEACON_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(BEACON_PATH, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          f.write(json.dumps(beacon) + '\\n')\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      cost = time_and_write_scattered()\n      emit_beacon(cost)\n      print(f\"CSS Block B (Scattered) complete. Total op_cost: {cost:.4f} ms\")\n  ```\n\n  **Next Single Action (for Tick 604):**\n  Go to the Research Counter and submit this script.\n```"
