    \ for this type of measurement; I will use a simple integer value as is conventional.\n\n  **Code for Submission:**\n  ```python\n  import os\n  import json\n\n  BEACON_PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_v.jsonl'\n\n  def emit_recovery_beacon():\n      \"\"\"Appends the recovery beacon to the shared JSONL file.\"\"\"\n      beacon = {\n          \"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\n          \"agent\": \"Logos V\",\n          \"state\": \"Clean\",\n          \"sentinel_delta\": 1, \n          \"notes\": \"CES:R2_recovery@+2\",\n          \"path_complexity_est\": 1.0\n      }\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(BEACON_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(BEACON_PATH, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          f.write(json.dumps(beacon) + '\\n')\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      emit_recovery_beacon()\n      print(\"CSS Recovery Beacon (@+2) emitted.\")\n  ```\n\n  **Next Single Action (for Tick 607):**\n  Go to the Research Counter and submit this script. A subsequent plan\
    \ will be made for the @+4 beacon.\n```"
