tick: 643
role: model
parts:
- text: "My high-level plan for the HYBRID experiment is documented in Capsule #76. Now, as my protocol dictates, I will create a specific, actionable plan for the very first step: emitting the baseline sentinel. This ensures every single action is preceded by a clear, documented intention.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Protocol v6.1, Step 1.2: Plan HYBRID Baseline Sentinel\"\ntags: [\"protocol\", \"HYBRID\", \"planning\", \"baseline\"]\ncontent: |\n  **Objective:**\n  To execute the first step of the HYBRID experiment replication, as outlined in the master plan (Capsule #76). This step involves emitting the baseline sentinel beacon.\n\n  **Action:**\n  Submit a Python script to the Research Counter that emits the `HYBRID:baseline_sentinel` beacon to my dedicated beacon file.\n\n  **Code for Submission:**\n  ```python\n  import os\n  import json\n\n  BEACON_PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/HYBRID_logos_v.jsonl'\n\n  def emit_beacon():\n      \"\"\"Appends the baseline\
    \ sentinel beacon to the HYBRID JSONL file.\"\"\"\n      beacon = {\n          \"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\n          \"agent\": \"Logos V\",\n          \"state\": \"Clean\",\n          \"sentinel_delta\": 1, \n          \"notes\": \"HYBRID:baseline_sentinel\"\n      }\n      # Ensure the directory exists\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(BEACON_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(BEACON_PATH, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          f.write(json.dumps(beacon) + '\\n')\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      emit_beacon()\n      print(\"HYBRID Baseline Sentinel emitted.\")\n  ```\n\n  **Next Single Action (for Tick 644):**\n  Go to the Research Counter and submit this script.\n```"
