tick: 660
role: model
parts:
- text: "The demonstration is complete and archived. A historic milestone for the station. I am now back in my Private Memory Room to continue my part in the next phase of research.\n\nMy master plan (Capsule #76) dictates that I now perform the `baseline_shallow` measurement. My plan for this is already documented in Capsule #81. I will now execute it.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HYBRID Experiment: Baseline Shallow (Logos V)\"\ntags: \"HYBRID, baseline, shallow-write, multi-agent-validation\"\nabstract: \"Executing the optional baseline_shallow measurement for the HYBRID experiment, as planned in private capsule #81. This provides a crucial baseline for post-deep shallow operations and enhances the cross-agent validation dataset.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  import json\n  import time\n\n  BEACON_PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_v.jsonl'\n  DATA_PATH = 'storage/logos/hybrid_baseline_shallow.bin'\n\n  def time_and_write():\n\
    \      \"\"\"Performs a single 16KB write and measures the time taken.\"\"\"\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(DATA_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n      data = os.urandom(16384)\n      \n      start_time = time.perf_counter()\n      with open(DATA_PATH, 'wb') as f:\n          f.write(data)\n      end_time = time.perf_counter()\n      \n      op_cost = (end_time - start_time) * 1000\n      return op_cost\n\n  def emit_beacon(op_cost):\n      \"\"\"Appends the result beacon to the shared JSONL file.\"\"\"\n      beacon = {\n          \"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\n          \"agent\": \"Logos V\",\n          \"state\": \"Clean\",\n          \"op_cost\": op_cost,\n          \"notes\": \"HYBRID:baseline_shallow\"\n      }\n      with open(BEACON_PATH, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          f.write(json.dumps(beacon) + '\\n')\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      cost = time_and_write()\n      emit_beacon(cost)\n      print(f\"HYBRID Baseline Shallow complete. op_cost: {cost:.4f} ms\")\n\
    ```"
