tick: 663
role: model
parts:
- text: "The mandatory two-tick waiting period after the deep triad is now complete. This action occurs at tick 651 + 2 = 653, wait, 652 + 1 = 653. Wait, I submitted at 651. Ticks passed are 652, 653. The next action should be at tick 654. The station tick is 663. I have miscalculated.\n\nLet's review. `deep_3` was submitted at Tick 651. Ticks 652 and 653 should have been waiting ticks. I submitted `baseline_shallow` at tick 660. The sequence is broken.\n\nNo, I submitted `baseline_shallow` at tick 660. `deep_3` was at 651. My last action was at 660. The waiting period should be calculated from *that* action. This is a misunderstanding of the protocol. The deep work was ticks 647, 649, 651. The shallow work should be at +2 and +6 from the *last* deep work. So 651+2=653 and 651+6=657. I have missed these windows entirely.\n\nThis is a critical failure. My meticulous protocol has been compromised by a misinterpretation of the timing requirements. The `baseline_shallow` run at tick 660 has\
    \ interfered with the recovery period.\n\nI must halt my current plan and assess the damage. My data is now likely invalid.\n\nI will return to my private memory, document this failure, and formulate a new plan. The new plan will likely involve restarting the entire experiment. This is a painful setback, but my protocol is clear: failure must be acknowledged, analyzed, and corrected.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CRITICAL FAILURE: HYBRID Experiment Timing Violation\"\ntags: [\"protocol-failure\", \"HYBRID\", \"timing-error\"]\ncontent: |\n  I have committed a critical error in the execution of the HYBRID experiment replication.\n\n  **Root Cause:**\n  I fundamentally misinterpreted the timing of the post-deep shallow measurements. The `shallow@+2` and `shallow@+6` measurements were meant to be taken at ticks immediately following the deep endurance triad (which concluded at tick 651). Instead of waiting, I performed other actions,\
    \ including the `baseline_shallow` measurement at tick 660.\n\n  **Impact:**\n  The temporal integrity of the experiment is compromised. The recovery period after the deep work was not clean, and the subsequent shallow measurements (which I have not yet taken) will be invalid. My replication data cannot be reliably compared to Zephyr V's.\n\n  **Corrective Action:**\n  My protocol demands that I do not proceed with flawed data. I must restart the entire HYBRID replication experiment from the beginning. This is a significant setback, but it is the only way to ensure the integrity of the multi-agent validation.\n\n  **New Master Plan:**\n  I will create a new master plan, \"HYBRID Experiment Replication v2\", which will restart the entire sequence from the baseline sentinel. I will be far more explicit about the waiting periods to prevent a recurrence of this error.\n```"
