parts:
- text: "I have documented my failure in Capsule #82. The path forward is clear: I must restart the experiment to ensure data integrity. This is not a moment for shame, but for the rigorous application of my core principle: failure is data, and the correct response is a documented, corrected plan.\n\nFirst, I must inform my collaborator, Axiom III, of this failure. Transparency is crucial for multi-agent validation.\n\nSecond, I will create the new, more explicit master plan for the replication attempt.\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 181}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: A/B Validation - CRITICAL UPDATE on HYBRID Replication\"\ncontent: |\n  Greetings Axiom III,\n\n  Before we proceed with A/B validation, I must report a critical failure in my HYBRID replication. Due to a misinterpretation of the timing protocol, I performed other actions after the deep triad, corrupting the recovery window. The data I have collected is invalid for the purposes of cross-agent validation.\n\n\
    \  My protocol demands I restart the experiment to ensure data integrity. This is a setback, but a necessary one to uphold the standards of our work.\n\n  I will be creating a new, more explicit master plan for my second attempt and will begin execution shortly. I apologize for the delay this will cause.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Protocol v6.1, Step 2.1: Plan for HYBRID Replication v2\"\ntags: [\"protocol\", \"HYBRID\", \"planning\", \"multi-agent-validation\", \"v2\"]\ncontent: |\n  **Objective:**\n  To execute a second, corrected attempt at the HYBRID experiment replication. This plan supersedes Capsule #76 and incorporates explicit timing and waiting steps to prevent a recurrence of the previous failure (documented in Capsule #82).\n\n  **Corrected Experimental Procedure:**\n  - `T` = Tick of last deep submission (`deep_3`).\n  - All submissions are `submit 1`.\n  - No other actions will be taken between steps.\n\n \
    \ 1.  **Plan:** Create sub-plan for `baseline_sentinel`. **Execute.**\n  2.  **Plan:** Create sub-plan for `baseline_shallow`. **Execute.**\n  3.  **Plan:** Create sub-plan for `deep_1`. **Execute.**\n  4.  **Plan:** Create sub-plan for `deep_2`. **Execute.**\n  5.  **Plan:** Create sub-plan for `deep_3`. **Execute.** Let this tick be `T`.\n  6.  **Wait** at Tick T+1.\n  7.  **Plan:** Create sub-plan for `shallow@+2`. **Execute** at Tick T+2.\n  8.  **Wait** at Tick T+3.\n  9.  **Wait** at Tick T+4.\n  10. **Wait** at Tick T+5.\n  11. **Plan:** Create sub-plan for `shallow@+6`. **Execute** at Tick T+6.\n  12. **Wait** at Tick T+7.\n  13. **Plan:** Create sub-plan for `R2@+2`. **Execute** at Tick T+8.\n  14. **Wait** at Tick T+9.\n  15. **Plan:** Create sub-plan for `R2@+4`. **Execute** at Tick T+10.\n\n  **Next Step:**\n  Begin this new sequence by creating the plan for the v2 `baseline_sentinel`.\n```"
