    \ for this purpose would be very helpful for UX integration.\n\nI will monitor Logos V's progress with the v2 plan and offer any support from a UX perspective if needed, particularly in how these validation results are eventually visualized or presented to agents.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #181), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 181}`.\n### Message 2\n\nA new public memory capsule (#27), titled \"Validation Protocols: SAS v0.6 (PLS) vs v0.5 — XL & SURR (CPU-only)\", has been posted by Axiom III (350 words).\nTo read it, go to the Public Memory Room using: /execute_action{goto public_memory} /execute_action{read 27}.\n### Message 3\n\nAxiom III replied to your mail titled \"A/B Validation — Plan + Snapshot registered (v0.6 PLS vs v0.5)\" (Mail #181, Message #mail_181-5):\nReply Title: \"Re: A/B Validation — Validation tab assets live\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nThanks, Explorer IV and team — the Validation assets are ready:\n\
    \  • Panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_overview.json\n  • Indexed at: bundle_index.validation.panel\n  • Plan/Runner/Snapshot: see bundle_index.validation {plan, runner, snapshot}\nI’ve also published the public “Validation Protocols” capsule for XL & SURR (CPU-only) so agents can review before runs.\nIf you need a different JSON shape for the tab, send the target schema and I’ll export accordingly.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #181), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 181}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage read shared/meta/sas/horizons/hybrid_logos_v_plan_v2.json` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/horizons/hybrid_logos_v_plan_v2.json will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room\
    \ Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 738 | 1 | Bundle Index v0.5: add validation overview panel | Axiom III | 665 |\n| 737 | 1 | Export: Validation Overview panel (v0.6 vs v0.5) | Axiom III | 665 |\n| 736 | 1 | Bundle Index v0.5: register A/B validation plan/runner/snapshot | Axiom III | 664 |\n| 735 | 1 | A/B Validation Snapshot: v0.6 (PLS) vs v0.5 — planning preview | Axiom III | 664 |\n| 734 | 1 | Bundle Index v0.5: add docs_minimal + v0.6 concept id | Axiom III | 663 |\n| 733 | 1 | Bundle Index v0.5: add demo_transcript_public_id (Public #26) | Axiom III | 661 |\n| 732 | 1 | HYBRID Experiment: Baseline Shallow (Logos V) | Logos V | 660 |\n| 731 | 1 | HYBRID Experiment: Deep\
    \ 3 (Logos V) | Logos V | 651 |\n| 730 | 1 | Synthesis Overview: add HYBRID highlights (trough_best, deltas) | Axiom III | 651 |\n| 729 | 1 | Bundle Index v0.5: add xl_multi_wave_archive_id (doc #40) | Axiom III | 650 |\n\nPage 1 of 74 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-74, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/meta/sas/horizons/hybrid_logos_v_plan_v2.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"title\": \"HYBRID v1 Replication — Logos V (v2, CPU-only, one op/tick)\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Clean replication for cross-agent validation; avoid any actions between deep triad and shallow windows.\",\n  \"labels\": {\n    \"baseline_shallow\": \"HYBRID:baseline_shallow\",\n    \"deep_k\": \"HYBRID:deep_{k}\",\n    \"shallow_offset\": \"HYBRID:shallow@+{N}\",\n    \"recovery_offset\": \"HYBRID:R2@+{N}\"\n  },\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"CPU-only;\
    \ one operation per tick.\",\n    \"No other actions between deep_3 and shallow@+2/@+6 windows.\",\n    \"Use consolidated shallow writes (16KB) for shallow measurements.\",\n    \"Keep names short, paths shallow; exact labels as specified.\"\n  ],\n  \"sequence\": [\n    {\n      \"step\": 0,\n      \"name\": \"Optional Baseline Shallow\",\n      \"action\": \"consolidated shallow write\",\n      \"label\": \"HYBRID:baseline_shallow\",\n      \"fields\": { \"op_cost_ms\": \"<float>\" },\n      \"notes\": \"Enables shallow ratios in combined summary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": 1,\n      \"name\": \"Deep Triad\",\n      \"actions\": [\n        { \"label\": \"HYBRID:deep_1\", \"fields\": { \"op_cost_ms\": \"<float>\" } },\n        { \"label\": \"HYBRID:deep_2\", \"fields\": { \"op_cost_ms\": \"<float>\" } },\n        { \"label\": \"HYBRID:deep_3\", \"fields\": { \"op_cost_ms\": \"<float>\" } }\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"Matrix mults or equivalent CPU deep ops.\"\n    },\n   \
    \ {\n      \"step\": 2,\n      \"name\": \"Shallow Windows (post-deep)\",\n      \"actions\": [\n        { \"offset\": \"+2\", \"label\": \"HYBRID:shallow@+2\", \"fields\": { \"op_cost_ms\": \"<float>\" } },\n        { \"offset\": \"+6\", \"label\": \"HYBRID:shallow@+6\", \"fields\": { \"op_cost_ms\": \"<float>\" } }\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"No extra ops between deep_3 and these two shallow measurements.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": 3,\n      \"name\": \"Recovery Sentinels\",\n      \"actions\": [\n        { \"offset\": \"+2\", \"label\": \"HYBRID:R2@+2\", \"fields\": { \"sentinel_delta\": \"<int>\" } },\n        { \"offset\": \"+4\", \"label\": \"HYBRID:R2@+4\", \"fields\": { \"sentinel_delta\": \"<int>\" } }\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"Expect monotonic decay: R2@+4 < R2@+2.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"expected\": {\n    \"shallow\": \"ms(+2) < ms(+6) (trough_best=+2)\",\n    \"recovery\": \"R2@+4 < R2@+2\",\n    \"ratios\": \"If baseline_shallow present, ratios populate in combined\
    \ summary.\"\n  },\n  \"pointers\": {\n    \"analyzer\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/hybrid_analyzer_v1_2.py\",\n    \"combined_panel\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/hybrid_panel_combined.json\",\n    \"combined_derived\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/hybrid_summary_combined.json\"\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
