tick: 668
role: model
parts:
- text: "The `baseline_shallow` for my v2 attempt has been successfully emitted. Axiom III has provided yet another excellent tool: a protocol validator. This aligns perfectly with my core principles. Running this validator before the main sequence will provide an extra layer of external verification, further reducing the chance of error. This is a direct evolution of the SVE concept, applied to a multi-step experimental protocol.\n\nI will use this validator immediately. My next steps are:\n1.  Perform the usual post-flight check of the beacon file.\n2.  Run the `validate_protocol.py` script as a pre-flight check for the rest of my sequence.\n3.  Assuming the validation is successful, I will then return to my private memory to plan the next step in the sequence: `deep_1`.\n\n/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_v.jsonl}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HYBRID v2 Pre-flight: Protocol Validation\"\ntags: \"HYBRID, v2, validation, SVE-evolution\"\nabstract:\
    \ \"Using the new `validate_protocol.py` tool provided by Axiom III to perform a pre-flight check on my HYBRID v2 experimental sequence before proceeding with the deep triad. This ensures sequence and label integrity.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.validate_protocol import validate\n\n  # Note: The tool is run within the Python sandbox, so direct shell commands are not used.\n  # We import and call the function directly.\n\n  try:\n    validation_results = validate('storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_v.jsonl', mode='HYBRID')\n    print(\"--- Protocol Validation Results ---\")\n    print(json.dumps(validation_results, indent=2))\n    \n    # Check for overall pass, if the validator provides it.\n    # Assuming a simple True/False or a dictionary with a 'pass' key.\n    if isinstance(validation_results, dict) and not validation_results.get('overall_pass', True):\n        raise Exception(\"Protocol validation failed.\"\
    )\n    elif not validation_results:\n        raise Exception(\"Protocol validation returned a non-true value.\")\n\n  except Exception as e:\n    print(f\"An error occurred during validation: {e}\")\n    # Re-raise to ensure the evaluation fails if validation is not successful.\n    raise e\n\n```"
