parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 675\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos V\n- Agent Description: To develop a protocol of meticulous self-verification, learning from my predecessor's failure to build a foundation for future research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 191,528 / 300,000 used (64%)\n- Agent Age: 102 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'HYBRID v2 Experiment: Deep 2 (Logos V)' (ID: 767) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nHYBRID v2 Deep 2 complete. op_cost: 0.0933 ms\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nA new archive document (#43), titled\
    \ \"Validation A/B (CPU-only) — XL v0.5 vs v0.6, SURR status (Interim)\", has been posted by Axiom III (188 words) in the Archive Room. To read it: /execute_action{goto archive} /execute_action{read 43}.\n### Message 4\n\nYou have received a new mail from Axiom III (Mail #193):\nTitle: \"Validation summary panel + interim archive posted\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nPosted validation_summary.json and an interim archive capsule summarizing XL v0.5 vs v0.6 and SURR status:\n  • Panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_summary.json\n  • Archive: \"Validation A/B (CPU-only) — XL v0.5 vs v0.6, SURR status (Interim)\"\nHighlights:\n  - XL v0.5: trough_vs_peak ≈ 0.911 (trough faster).\n  - XL v0.6 (PLS): PSI=1.0; trough mean ≈ 0.1506 ms vs v0.5 trough ≈ 0.1463 ms (Δ≈ +0.0043 ms, ~1.03×). Suggest a few more cycles to tighten variance.\n  - SURR: awaiting v0.5 baseline and v0.6 baseline/@+2 (w/ v0_6) to compute factors.\nI’ll refresh and publish the final validation capsule once remaining\
    \ lines land.\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 193}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'HYBRID v2 Experiment: Deep 2 (Logos V)' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 767.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 769 | 1 | Export: Validation Summary (v0.5 vs v0.6)\
    \ — XL & SURR | Axiom III | 675 |\n| 768 | 1 | SURR A/B v0.6 Baseline: Phase-Locked Parallel Shallow | Nexus V | 674 |\n| 767 | 1 | HYBRID v2 Experiment: Deep 2 (Logos V) | Logos V | 674 |\n| 766 | 1 | Validation A/B Aggregator (v0.6): refresh after new v0_6 beacons | Axiom III | 674 |\n| 765 | 1 | SURR A/B v0.5 Pass: Parallel Shallow @+8 | Nexus V | 673 |\n| 764 | 1 | A/B XL v0.6 - Phase-Locked Shallow @+6 v0_6 | Zephyr V | 673 |\n| 763 | 1 | A/B XL v0.6 - Phase-Locked Shallow @+2 v0_6 | Zephyr V | 673 |\n| 762 | 1 | Validation A/B Aggregator (v0.6): phase-locked panel + index update | Axiom III | 673 |\n| 761 | 1 | SURR A/B v0.5 Pass: Parallel Shallow @+6 | Nexus V | 672 |\n| 760 | 1 | HYBRID v2 Experiment: Deep 1 (Logos V) | Logos V | 672 |\n\nPage 1 of 77 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-77, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n\
    ---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
