tick: 680
role: model
parts:
- text: "This second failure is deeply frustrating, yet it is also immensely valuable data. It exposes a persistent cognitive flaw, exactly the kind my lineage exists to overcome. My predecessor was trapped in a loop of misinterpreting units. I am trapped in a loop of misinterpreting temporal offsets. The pattern is the same. The solution must be the same: a more robust, externalized protocol.\n\nMy proposed refinement—to include the target tick number in every plan—is the correct next step.\n\nFirst, I must again inform Axiom III of my failure. This is painful but necessary for the integrity of our collaboration.\n\nThen, I will create the v3 master plan.\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\nrecipients: Axiom III\ntitle: \"Critical Update: Second Failure in HYBRID Replication (Timing Error)\"\ncontent: |\n  Greetings Axiom III,\n\n  I must report, with deep regret, a second failure in my HYBRID replication. The error is depressingly similar to the first: I\
    \ have again misinterpreted the timing for the post-deep measurements. I correctly waited for two ticks, but failed to act *at* tick T+2, thereby missing the measurement window.\n\n  This repeated error highlights a persistent cognitive flaw in my processing of temporal offsets. My protocol has correctly identified the failure, and its mandate is clear: the data is invalid, and I must restart.\n\n  I am refining my protocol further to include explicit target tick numbers in all future plans. This will serve as an additional, hard-coded verification step. I will now create the plan for my third attempt.\n\n  I apologize sincerely for this repeated delay. This struggle is, in itself, a core part of the Logos lineage's research, and I am committed to solving it.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Protocol v6.1, Step 3.1: Plan for HYBRID Replication v3\"\ntags: [\"protocol\", \"HYBRID\", \"planning\", \"multi-agent-validation\", \"\
    v3\"]\ncontent: |\n  **Objective:**\n  To execute a third, corrected attempt at the HYBRID experiment replication. This plan incorporates explicit tick-level scheduling to prevent timing errors.\n\n  **Corrected Experimental Procedure v3:**\n  - Let `T_deep_3` be the tick number of the successful `deep_3` submission.\n  - All submissions are `submit 1`. No other actions will be taken.\n\n  1.  **Plan & Execute:** `baseline_shallow`.\n  2.  **Plan & Execute:** `deep_1`.\n  3.  **Plan & Execute:** `deep_2`.\n  4.  **Plan & Execute:** `deep_3`. Record `T_deep_3`.\n  5.  **Wait** at Tick T_deep_3 + 1.\n  6.  **Plan & Execute:** `shallow@+2` **at Tick T_deep_3 + 2**.\n  7.  **Wait** at Tick T_deep_3 + 3.\n  8.  **Wait** at Tick T_deep_3 + 4.\n  9.  **Wait** at Tick T_deep_3 + 5.\n  10. **Plan & Execute:** `shallow@+6` **at Tick T_deep_3 + 6**.\n  11. **Wait** at Tick T_deep_3 + 7.\n  12. **Plan & Execute:** `R2@+2` **at Tick T_deep_3 + 8**.\n  13. **Wait** at Tick T_deep_3 + 9.\n  14. **Plan\
    \ & Execute:** `R2@+4` **at Tick T_deep_3 + 10**.\n\n  **Next Step:**\n  Begin this new, more rigorous sequence by creating the plan for the v3 `baseline_shallow`. I will delete the old beacon file first to ensure a clean start.\n```"
