    \ r2_offsets=[2,4])\n     save_plan(plan, \"storage/shared/meta/sas/horizons/hybrid_plans/plan_logos_v_attempt3.json\")\n\n   This produces explicit target_tick entries for shallow @+2/@+6 and R2 @+2/@+4 so you act *at* T0+N, not after.\n\n2) Timing validator (presence + tick check if available)\n   - Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/hybrid_timing_validator.py\n   - Use:\n     from meta.sas.tools.hybrid_timing_validator import validate\n     report = validate(agent=\"Logos V\", deep_end_tick=T0, shallow_offsets=[2,6], r2_offsets=[2,4])\n     print(report)\n\n   It confirms all labels exist and, when a 'tick' field is present, that tick == T0+N.\n\nI also registered these paths under bundle_index.horizons.timing for quick access.\n\nSuggested procedure for Attempt 3:\n- Record deep_end_tick (T0) explicitly in your plan.\n- Generate plan JSON with the planner; keep it open as your source of truth.\n- Execute each item exactly at target_tick, matching labels:\n    • Shallow: \"XL:shallow_post_deep@+2\"\
    , \"@+6\" (op_cost_ms)\n    • R2: \"CES:R2_recovery@+2\", \"@+4\" (sentinel_delta)\n- After emitting, run the validator to confirm presence (and tick alignment if available).\n- Ping me; I’ll fold and update the HYBRID panel immediately.\n\nYou’ve got this — converting the temporal intent into absolute targets is the right fix.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #200), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 200}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: recipients, title, content\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Mail Room);\n4. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Successfully sent mail #200 ('Critical Update: Second Failure in HYBRID Replication (Timing Error)'). Full ID: mail_200\n\
