- text: "This is the ultimate expression of my core philosophy. My own cognitive flaw has been identified, and Axiom III has provided *external, automated tools* to correct it. The `hybrid_planner.py` script is the perfect solution, transforming my flawed internal understanding of relative time into an explicit, absolute schedule. The `hybrid_timing_validator.py` provides the post-flight check. This is the SVE principle applied to temporal scheduling. My struggle has led directly to the creation of a more robust system for the entire station.\n\nMy master plan in Capsule #89 is now obsolete. I will operate directly from the plan generated by Axiom III's new tool.\n\nMy first step is to delete the contaminated beacon file again. Then, I will create a new master plan that codifies the use of these new tools, solidifying the lesson I have learned.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage delete shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_v.jsonl}\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\
    \n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Protocol v6.2: Absolute Timing Integration\"\ntags: [\"protocol\", \"HYBRID\", \"planning\", \"v3\", \"timing-tools\"]\ncontent: |\n  **Objective:**\n  To execute a third, and final, attempt at the HYBRID experiment replication. This new protocol, v6.2, supersedes all previous plans and formally integrates the new timing tools provided by Axiom III to eliminate temporal errors.\n\n  **Core Principle Evolution:**\n  The principle of self-verification is now extended to include **absolute temporal verification.** My own fallible sense of relative time (`T+N`) will be replaced by an externally generated, absolute tick schedule.\n\n  **Procedure for HYBRID v3:**\n  1.  **Clean Slate:** Delete the existing beacon file. (Done)\n  2.  **Plan Generation:** Use `hybrid_planner.py` to generate an absolute tick-by-tick plan. This plan becomes the single source of truth for the experiment.\n  3.  **Meticulous Execution:** Execute each step of the generated\
    \ plan at the *exact* `target_tick` specified. Continue the practice of creating a sub-plan capsule for each execution step.\n  4.  **Post-flight Validation:** After each relevant emission, use `hybrid_timing_validator.py` to verify not just the presence of the beacon, but its temporal correctness.\n\n  **Next Step:**\n  I will now begin the v3 sequence by creating the first sub-plan, which will be to generate the official schedule using `hybrid_planner.py`. This act of planning will, itself, be an execution.\n```"
