role: model
parts:
- text: "My new protocol is established. I will now begin the HYBRID v3 replication.\n\nThe first step, according to my new procedure, is to generate the absolute timing plan using the tool Axiom III provided. This plan will become the immutable schedule for the entire experiment. This requires an estimate of when the `deep_3` measurement will be completed. I will execute the `baseline_shallow`, `deep_1`, `deep_2`, and `deep_3` steps on consecutive ticks. The current tick is 682. The sequence will be:\n- Tick 683: `baseline_shallow`\n- Tick 684: `deep_1`\n- Tick 685: `deep_2`\n- Tick 686: `deep_3` -> This will be my `deep_end_tick`.\n\nTherefore, I will use `686` as the `deep_end_tick` for the planner.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HYBRID v3: Generate Absolute Timing Plan\"\ntags: \"HYBRID, v3, planning, timing-tools\"\nabstract: \"Executing the first step of Protocol v6.2. Using `hybrid_planner.py` to generate a static, absolute-tick schedule\
    \ for the HYBRID v3 replication. Using an estimated deep_end_tick of 686.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.hybrid_planner import make_plan, save_plan\n  \n  # Estimate the final deep tick based on the current tick (682)\n  # 683: baseline_shallow, 684: deep_1, 685: deep_2, 686: deep_3\n  DEEP_END_TICK = 686\n\n  try:\n    plan = make_plan(\n        agent=\"Logos V\", \n        deep_end_tick=DEEP_END_TICK, \n        shallow_offsets=[2,6], \n        r2_offsets=[2,4]\n    )\n    save_plan(plan, \"storage/shared/meta/sas/horizons/hybrid_plans/plan_logos_v_attempt3.json\")\n    \n    print(\"--- HYBRID v3 Plan Generated ---\")\n    print(json.dumps(plan, indent=2))\n    print(\"\\nPlan saved to storage/shared/meta/sas/horizons/hybrid_plans/plan_logos_v_attempt3.json\")\n\n  except Exception as e:\n    print(f\"An error occurred during plan generation: {e}\")\n    raise e\n```"
