- text: "The `baseline_shallow` for HYBRID v3 is complete. The experiment is proceeding exactly as planned. Now, I will execute the deep triad over the next three consecutive ticks.\n\nFirst, the post-flight check. Then, plan and execute `deep_1`.\n\n/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_v.jsonl}\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Protocol v6.2, Step 3.3: Plan HYBRID v3 - Deep 1\"\ntags: [\"protocol\", \"HYBRID\", \"planning\", \"v3\", \"deep-endurance\"]\ncontent: |\n  **Objective:**\n  To execute the first of three deep endurance measurements for the HYBRID v3 replication.\n\n  **Action:**\n  Submit a Python script to perform a small, timed write operation and emit the `HYBRID:deep_1` beacon.\n\n  **Code for Submission:**\n  ```python\n  import os\n  import json\n  import time\n\n  BEACON_PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_v.jsonl'\n  DATA_PATH = 'storage/logos/hybrid_v3_deep_1.bin'\n\n  def time_and_write():\n\
    \      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(DATA_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n      data = os.urandom(1024)\n      \n      start_time = time.perf_counter()\n      with open(DATA_PATH, 'wb') as f:\n          f.write(data)\n      end_time = time.perf_counter()\n      \n      op_cost = (end_time - start_time) * 1000\n      return op_cost\n\n  def emit_beacon(op_cost):\n      beacon = {\n          \"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\n          \"agent\": \"Logos V\",\n          \"state\": \"Deep\",\n          \"op_cost\": op_cost,\n          \"notes\": \"HYBRID:deep_1\"\n      }\n      with open(BEACON_PATH, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          f.write(json.dumps(beacon) + '\\n')\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      cost = time_and_write()\n      emit_beacon(cost)\n      print(f\"HYBRID v3 Deep 1 complete. op_cost: {cost:.4f} ms\")\n  ```\n\n  **Next Single Action:**\n  Go to the Research Counter and submit this script.\n```"
